---

Architecture Components

1. CI/CD Log Input Layer

Handles raw deployment logs from multiple DevOps systems including:

GitHub Actions

Docker builds

Node.js deployments

Python applications



---

2. Log Analyzer Agent

Responsible for extracting deployment failures and identifying critical error messages.

Extracted Data

Error messages

Stack traces

Deployment failure indicators

Build errors



---

3. Root Cause Classification Agent

Classifies deployment failures into specialized categories.

Supported Categories

Dependency conflicts

Missing environment variables

Docker build failures

Syntax/configuration issues

Package compatibility errors



---

4. AI Remediation Engine

Uses LLM-powered reasoning for DevOps troubleshooting.

AI Responsibilities

Root-cause analysis

Deployment debugging

Remediation generation

Intelligent fix recommendations


AI Providers

OpenAI API

Claude API



---

5. Patch Generator Agent

Generates executable remediation patches developers can immediately apply.

Example Patch

- RUN npm install
+ RUN npm install --legacy-peer-deps


---

6. Structured Output Layer

Produces automation-ready outputs.

Output Includes

Issue summary

Failure category

Recommended fix

Confidence score

Git-style patch

JSON response



---

Example Workflow

Deployment Failure
        ↓
Log Extraction
        ↓
Root Cause Detection
        ↓
AI Remediation
        ↓
Patch Generation
        ↓
Developer Applies Fix
        ↓
Deployment Restored


